meta {
  name: Stream variant playlist
  type: http
  seq: 12
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/videos/{{videoId}}/stream/{{rendition}}.m3u8
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{accessToken}}
}

vars:pre-request {
  rendition: 720p
}

docs {
  One rendition's playlist. Every segment line is replaced by a presigned GET URL that storage honours for `STREAM_URL_TTL_SECONDS` (default 300). After that the same URL returns 403 `AccessDenied`, so a copied link stops working within 5 minutes.

  `rendition` must be `master` or match `^\d{3,4}p$`. Anything else, including `..%2Fsecret`, is a 400. A rendition the video doesn't have is a 404 `RENDITION_NOT_FOUND`.

  Example response (shortened):

  ```text
  #EXTM3U
  #EXT-X-VERSION:6
  #EXT-X-TARGETDURATION:6
  #EXT-X-MEDIA-SEQUENCE:0
  #EXT-X-PLAYLIST-TYPE:VOD
  #EXT-X-INDEPENDENT-SEGMENTS
  #EXTINF:6.000000,
  http://localhost:9000/hls-output/4dce8038-.../720p/seg_000.ts?X-Amz-Algorithm=AWS4-HMAC-SHA256&X-Amz-Expires=300&X-Amz-Signature=...
  #EXTINF:6.000000,
  http://localhost:9000/hls-output/4dce8038-.../720p/seg_001.ts?X-Amz-Algorithm=AWS4-HMAC-SHA256&X-Amz-Expires=300&X-Amz-Signature=...
  ...
  #EXT-X-ENDLIST
  ```

  A VOD playlist is read once, so a player that keeps going past the TTL must fetch this playlist again when a segment returns 403. The dev player does exactly that.
}
